  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In Toulon's western districts, near Pont du Las, Parc des Cèdres offers a green space of 0.66 hectare (about 6,600 m² according to the City of Toulon), with a playground and a pétanque court in addition to the dog area. A pleasant setting for a family walk, more intimate than the city's large parks.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park officially appears in the municipal document "Toulon, ville amie des chiens": lead required, dedicated dog area confirmed by an official source. The park, of modest size, suits a quiet stroll better than a big sporting outing.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: a good neighbourhood spot for a green break between errands, no need to plan a whole afternoon around it.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Toulon's western districts and the Pont du Las area are right nearby, handy for working this break into an urban walk.</p>
